comments[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-22T10:28:24.200Z",codex-agent,"PR 266 review round: created the requested worktree, pulled the remote head and merged origin/main before changes. npm ci passed with zero audit vulnerabilities. All four unresolved threads and every comment read; latest CodeRabbit body has no outside-diff section. Rechecked main ff1418fff98b4409421053a44e46e488f11daa64 and merged PR 247 audit: package-search boundary was delivered by PR 215/a102d18, not PR 247. Five release closures use unrelated copied evidence; replace each with its actual delivering commit and relevant workflow/package/test files. Entry text uses nonblank close_reason only with --entry-from close_reason; default and blank fallback use title, subject to neutral-closure policy. Correct all affected current fields through pinned pm updates, rename the source title for generated changelog grammar, and verify append-only histories. Do not newly close any item."
  "2026-10-22T10:33:01.258Z",codex-agent,"Tracker-only evidence proof: full before/after reads each certified complete with 190/190 rows, no omissions, unreadable items or continuation. Rechecked all 14 delivery/follow-up commit references as ancestors of main ff1418fff98b4409421053a44e46e488f11daa64 and all 15 retained evidence paths on that main tree. Seven corrected current records match the per-item source evidence; their status, closed_at and completed_at remain unchanged. All 13 pre-round PR history streams retain their original bytes as prefixes. pm history <id> --verify --json passed 14/14 chains including the review item, all current_matches_latest true. The linked pm history test also passed 1/1 commands. No code-function revert applies to this tracker-only change. Self-review found the same unrelated retained-evidence reference in pmc-wf7n and corrected it too; no other false delivery attribution found among the 13 reconciled records. The source title correction will regenerate the requested changelog grammar. Serialized health after writes has only existing pm-github host-version skew and exact 32-event legacy provenance baseline; an overlapping health read briefly reported drift, cleared when writers finished. No history repair or new closure event."
  "2026-10-22T10:35:00.154Z",codex-agent,"Tracker-only gates passed: npm ci (zero audit vulnerabilities), npm run changelog:full and npm run changelog:check (including links). Generated CHANGELOG.md differs by exactly the requested verifier clause. pm health --json --require-merge-drivers exits 0 with only the existing clone-local extension-host version skew and exact 32-event legacy provenance baseline; no durable history drift or pending merge receipts. All 14 history chains verify with current_matches_latest true; all 13 existing stream prefixes remain byte-identical. The linked history test passed. Full PR self-review retains only .agents/pm and CHANGELOG.md relative to main; no runtime function or distribution changes. All four findings are valid and fixed. No new PM CLI/SDK bug established; the overlapping health observation cleared in the serialized repeat. Release review claim without closing it or any other item; final changelog/link and health verification repeats after this final tracker write."
